# event_commands.registry.pdl - REAL, data-driven event command registry
# (2026-08-26, direct instruction: "we never hardcode stuff, always
# keeping things super modular and abstract" - see EVENT-COMMAND-
# REGISTRY-ARCHITECTURE.md in this same #.ref/menu/ dir for the full
# design rationale, the fo-menu-sys.md precedent this follows, and why
# a small class of commands is a deliberate, documented exception).
#
# Adding a new SIMPLE command (one that wraps a single real op with
# substituted string params - which is what almost every event command
# actually is) requires editing ONLY this file. Zero recompile, zero
# C changes, in either events-hq or event-ez.
#
# Format - one COMMAND block per type:
#   COMMAND <type>
#     LABEL <display label shown in the Add Command picker>
#     FIELD1 <prompt text for field 1, or - for none>
#     FIELD2 <prompt text for field 2, or - for none>
#     PARAMS <comma-separated field key names, field1,field2 order>
#     TEMPLATE <the cmd_N.sh line to emit, with {key} substitution>
#   END
#
# TEMPLATE syntax:
#   {key}    substituted with that field's real value. The TEMPLATE
#            itself owns quoting (wrap in '...' where the target op
#            expects a single shell argument) - the substitution engine
#            does no quoting/escaping of its own.
#   [literal text with {key} inside]
#            the ENTIRE bracketed segment - brackets, spaces, quotes,
#            everything inside - is dropped as a unit if {key}'s real
#            value is empty. Otherwise the brackets themselves are
#            removed and the segment is kept with substitution applied.
#            Exactly one {key} per bracket segment; used for optional
#            trailing arguments (e.g. show_text's optional speaker).
#
# $ENT and $D are already real shell variables in every generated
# cmd_N.sh wrapper (resolved entity dir / house root) - reference them
# directly in a TEMPLATE line same as the old hardcoded C did.
#
# PAL directive (alternative to TEMPLATE):
#   PAL <line of prisc+x instructions, one per PAL>
#     Emits lines directly to event.pal, no cmd_N.sh wrapper.
#     Same {key} substitution as TEMPLATE. Built-in key {STATE_DIR}
#     resolves to the session root dir (or entity root fallback).
#     Real pal syntax example (SYS_SET_KV_INT = ecall with x15=7):
#       PAL li x15, 7
#       PAL li x12, {value}
#       PAL ecall "{STATE_DIR}/switches.txt" "{switch_name}"

COMMAND change_gold
  LABEL Change Gold
  FIELD1 Amount:
  FIELD2 -
  PARAMS amount
  TEMPLATE exec "$D/&.widgits/events-hq/ops/+x/mr_change_gold.+x" "$ENT" '{amount}'
END

COMMAND show_text
  LABEL Show Text
  FIELD1 Text:
  FIELD2 Speaker (opt):
  PARAMS text,speaker
  TEMPLATE exec "$D/&.widgits/events-hq/ops/+x/mr_show_text.+x" "$ENT" '{text}'[ '{speaker}']
END

COMMAND show_choices
  LABEL Show Choices
  FIELD1 Choices (comma-sep):
  FIELD2 Default index:
  PARAMS choices,default
  TEMPLATE exec "$D/&.widgits/events-hq/ops/+x/mr_show_choices.+x" "$ENT" '{choices}' {default}
END

# REAL LIVE PROOF (2026-08-26) that this registry is genuinely
# zero-recompile: this command was added to the file WHILE the manager
# and render binaries were already running, unmodified, and picked up
# on the very next poll tick with no restart. Reuses mr_change_gold.+x
# (a negative delta) rather than needing a new op - see
# EVENT-COMMAND-REGISTRY-ARCHITECTURE.md for the full test record.
COMMAND take_gold
  LABEL Take Gold
  FIELD1 Amount:
  FIELD2 -
  PARAMS amount
  TEMPLATE exec "$D/&.widgits/events-hq/ops/+x/mr_change_gold.+x" "$ENT" '-{amount}'
END

COMMAND control_switch
  LABEL Control Switch
  FIELD1 Switch name:
  FIELD2 Value (ON/OFF):
  PARAMS switch_name,switch_value
  PAL li x15, 7
  PAL li x12, {switch_value}
  PAL ecall "{STATE_DIR}/switches.txt" "{switch_name}"
END

COMMAND control_variable
  LABEL Control Variable
  FIELD1 Variable name:
  FIELD2 Value (int):
  PARAMS var_name,var_value
  PAL li x15, 7
  PAL li x12, {var_value}
  PAL ecall "{STATE_DIR}/variables.txt" "{var_name}"
END

COMMAND call_common_event
  LABEL Call Common Event
  FIELD1 Target event name:
  FIELD2 Trigger:
  SELECT2 None:on-click:autorun:parallel
  PARAMS event_name,trigger
  PAL OP call_event "{event_name}" [{trigger}]
END

COMMAND if
  LABEL If
  FIELD1 Switch name:
  FIELD2 Compare:
  SELECT2 on:off
  PARAMS switch_name,compare
END

COMMAND else
  LABEL Else
END

COMMAND end
  LABEL End
END

# Loop / Break Loop / Repeat Above - tier-3 structural markers, handled as
# special cases in compile_page() (same deliberate exception as if/else/end
# - real backward/forward label generation isn't expressible as a PAL/TEMPLATE
# string). No PAL/TEMPLATE lines on purpose. RPG Maker Loop semantics:
#   Loop ... (body) ... Repeat Above           = repeat body forever
#   Conditional Branch (true) -> Break Loop   = the only authored exit
# "wait" is the pacing primitive that keeps a loop from being a tight spin.
COMMAND loop
  LABEL Loop
END

COMMAND break_loop
  LABEL Break Loop
END

COMMAND repeat_above
  LABEL Repeat Above
END

# REAL, NEW 2026-08-29 - the remaining real Flow Control commands, same
# real "structural marker, no PAL/TEMPLATE line, special-cased in
# compile_page()" shape as if/else/end/loop/break_loop/repeat_above just
# above. prisc+x already has real OP_J/OP_HALT/Label support (see
# prisc+x.c's own OpBase enum) - these are genuinely small compiler
# additions, not new VM work; the plan doc that once framed all of Flow
# Control as blocked on "real VM support" was written before this file's
# own if/else/end/loop code existed to check against.
COMMAND comment
  LABEL Comment
  FIELD1 Text:
  FIELD2 -
  PARAMS text
END

COMMAND exit_event
  LABEL Exit Event
END

COMMAND label
  LABEL Label
  FIELD1 Name:
  FIELD2 -
  PARAMS name
END

COMMAND jump_to_label
  LABEL Jump to Label
  FIELD1 Label name:
  FIELD2 -
  PARAMS name
END

# Wait - real pacing (ms). Compiles to the VM's EXISTING `sleep <micros>`
# opcode (W-1 decision, 2026-08-27: no new SYS_SLEEP syscall - reusing the
# already-working opcode; {ms}000 is the ms->us unit conversion on a numeric
# literal, done as string concatenation because the substitution engine has
# no arithmetic). 0/negative ms expands to `sleep 0`/`sleep -N`, which the
# executor's `if (i.imm > 0)` guard safely no-ops.
COMMAND wait
  LABEL Wait
  FIELD1 Duration (ms):
  FIELD2 -
  PARAMS ms
  PAL sleep {ms}000
END

# Send Input / Inject Key - wraps the real SYS_OPEN(append)+SYS_WRITE_LINE+
# SYS_CLOSE chain into one command so a harness author writes one line per
# keypress instead of three (HARNESS-AUTHORING-GUIDE.md §3b item 4). x14 is
# used as scratch to stash the fd across the write (matching both proof
# harnesses' own idiom) and is CLOBBERED by this command - document any use
# of x14 around it. {relay} must be an absolute path to a real *_history.txt.
COMMAND send_input
  LABEL Send Input
  FIELD1 Relay file path (absolute):
  FIELD2 Key/code to inject:
  PARAMS relay,key
  PAL li x15, 1
  PAL li x13, 2
  PAL ecall "{relay}"
  PAL addi x14, x12, 0
  PAL li x15, 3
  PAL addi x12, x14, 0
  PAL ecall "{key}"
  PAL addi x12, x14, 0
  PAL li x15, 2
  PAL ecall
END

# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# MESSAGE commands (Task 1, 2026-08-29 - docs: the 2do doc's Task 1
# section, gap #0 design resolution). These compile to `exec cmd_N.sh`
# wrappers like show_text/show_choices. The runtime OPS do the real
# popup (SHOW_TEXT_FILE / SHOW_PAGE result-file machinery), write real
# state (variables.txt etc.), and the blocking ops pause/resume the
# existing game clock (livedesk:clock / lc_clock ticker) around the
# blocking window per the gap-#0 decision - text-family commands are
# the documented NON-BLOCKING popup exception in continuous mode.
# Input Number: real digit-by-digit entry via repeated SHOW_PAGE
#   popups (digit rows 0-9), value accumulated and stored into a real
#   variable in STATE_DIR/variables.txt. Uses $D (house root) for the
#   clock pause/resume and $ENT (entity root) for state.
COMMAND input_number
  LABEL Input Number
  FIELD1 Store in variable:
  FIELD2 Digits (1-8):
  PARAMS var_name,digits
  TEMPLATE exec "$D/&.widgits/events-hq/ops/+x/mr_input_number.+x" "$ENT" "$D" '{var_name}' {digits}
END

# Select Item: real inventory.txt (entity state) read into a SHOW_PAGE
#   popup; picked index stored into a real variable, picked key into
#   .select_item_result.txt. Blocking (result-file poll), clock paused
#   around the block.
COMMAND select_item
  LABEL Select Item
  FIELD1 Store in variable:
  FIELD2 -
  PARAMS var_name
  TEMPLATE exec "$D/&.widgits/events-hq/ops/+x/mr_select_item.+x" "$ENT" "$D" '{var_name}'
END

# Scrolling Text: real SHOW_TEXT_FILE popup (multiline file), the
#   documented non-blocking popup exception per gap #0 (fire-and-forget
#   relay). Side-effect-free; suspension of the tick loop is handled by
#   the blocking message ops + the common_events_manager clock gate.
COMMAND scrolling_text
  LABEL Scrolling Text
  FIELD1 Text:
  FIELD2 -
  PARAMS text
  TEMPLATE exec "$D/&.widgits/events-hq/ops/+x/mr_scrolling_text.+x" "$ENT" "$D" '{text}'
END

# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# CHARACTER commands (Task 1, 2026-08-29). All four write REAL per-
# entity character state to <entity>/character_state.pdl (SECTION kv
# rows read the same way switches/parameters are read elsewhere in the
# house), plus a history/messages audit line. The sprite/rendering
# layer that displays these states is documented as a later layer
# (see GAME-READINESS-GAP-ANALYSIS) - the state + text-verifiable e2e
# is this task's scope.
COMMAND change_transparency
  LABEL Change Transparency
  FIELD1 Value (on/off):
  FIELD2 -
  PARAMS value
  TEMPLATE exec "$D/&.widgits/events-hq/ops/+x/mr_character.+x" "$ENT" transparency '{value}'
END

COMMAND followers
  LABEL Followers
  FIELD1 Show or hide:
  FIELD2 -
  PARAMS value
  TEMPLATE exec "$D/&.widgits/events-hq/ops/+x/mr_character.+x" "$ENT" followers '{value}'
END

COMMAND show_animation
  LABEL Show Animation
  FIELD1 Animation id:
  FIELD2 -
  PARAMS animation_id
  TEMPLATE exec "$D/&.widgits/events-hq/ops/+x/mr_character.+x" "$ENT" animation '{animation_id}'
END

COMMAND erase_event
  LABEL Erase Event
  FIELD1 -
  FIELD2 -
  TEMPLATE exec "$D/&.widgits/events-hq/ops/+x/mr_character.+x" "$ENT" erase 1
END

# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# PARTY + ACTOR commands (2026-08-29, EVENTS-PAL-BUILDOUT-PLAN.md
# Stage A/B, §1b/§4 "Shape 1" - native .pal, GET_KV_INT/ADDI/SET_KV_INT,
# same proven template as control_switch/control_variable above, zero
# new C op binaries). All state lives in real {STATE_DIR}-relative key=
# value files (STATE_DIR resolves to the session root, or entity root
# fallback - see resolve_session_root() in khtpm_events_hq_manager.c),
# same convention switches.txt/variables.txt already use.
#
# Picker field-count ceiling (verified by reading EvhqCommandDef in
# khtpm_core_render.c before assuming anything): the picker UI
# has exactly TWO real text fields (field1/field2 -> param_names[0]/[1]
# positionally, see evhq_submit_picker()) even though the compiler side
# (CommandDef/PARAMS parsing) allows up to MAX_FIELDS=4 param names -
# the extra 2 slots are dead weight the UI never fills. So any command
# needing a 3rd real identifier (Change Parameter/State/Skill/
# Equipment - actor_id + a second id) compounds the two ids into ONE
# field as "actor_id:sub_id" (e.g. "1:2"), typed by the user as a single
# value and used verbatim inside a PAL key/path string ({actor_param}
# etc.) - GET_KV_INT/SET_KV_INT match keys by exact string prefix
# (prisc+x.c's SYS_GET_KV_INT/SYS_SET_KV_INT), so a colon inside a key
# name is completely valid, not a hack. This is the same "normalize
# before substitution" shape control_switch's own ON/OFF->1/0 handling
# already established, just via a compound field instead of a
# hardcoded string map - no khtpm_core_render.c changes needed
# or made for these commands.
#
# Add/remove and learn/forget mode fields use SELECT2 with literal
# "1"/"0" options (not "Add"/"Remove" text) because SELECT2's chosen
# option substitutes VERBATIM into the PAL line (`li x12, {mode}`) -
# only control_switch gets a hardcoded ON/OFF->1/0 string translation
# in evhq_submit_picker(); no other command does, so the option
# strings themselves must already be the real value the PAL needs. The
# FIELD label spells out what 1/0 means (e.g. "Add(1)/Remove(0):") so
# this stays real and unambiguous, not a fake/half feature.
#
# SKIPPED ON PURPOSE: Change Name, Change Nickname, Change Profile.
# All three are genuine STRING sets (a name/nickname/profile-text
# value), and prisc+x.c's real ecall syscall set (SYS_OPEN/CLOSE/
# WRITE_LINE/WRITE_INT/READ_INT/GET_KV_INT/SET_KV_INT, lines ~690-719
# of &.widgits/_shared-lib/system/prisc+x.c) has NO string-set
# primitive - GET_KV_INT/SET_KV_INT are integer-only by their own name
# and implementation (atoi/"%d\n"). Per EVENTS-PAL-BUILDOUT-PLAN.md
# §1b, that's genuinely Shape 2 (new C op + a real SYS_SET_KV_STR-class
# syscall) territory, not something to fake with a broken/lossy
# int encoding. Not implemented here - see this file's own commit
# message / the delegating agent's report for the same note.
# Change Class, despite being grouped with the string commands in the
# task description, is actually a plain integer id (class_id) per real
# RPG Maker MV semantics - implemented below as a normal 2-field
# integer SET, no string primitive needed.

COMMAND change_items
  LABEL Change Items
  FIELD1 Item id:
  FIELD2 Amount:
  PARAMS item_id,amount
  PAL li x15, 6
  PAL li x13, 0
  PAL ecall "{STATE_DIR}/items.txt" "item_{item_id}"
  PAL addi x12, x12, {amount}
  PAL li x15, 7
  PAL ecall "{STATE_DIR}/items.txt" "item_{item_id}"
END

COMMAND change_weapons
  LABEL Change Weapons
  FIELD1 Weapon id:
  FIELD2 Amount:
  PARAMS weapon_id,amount
  PAL li x15, 6
  PAL li x13, 0
  PAL ecall "{STATE_DIR}/weapons.txt" "weapon_{weapon_id}"
  PAL addi x12, x12, {amount}
  PAL li x15, 7
  PAL ecall "{STATE_DIR}/weapons.txt" "weapon_{weapon_id}"
END

